00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.060
Leah: Let’s look at Media
influences in a little more detail.

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:07.199
Mental health and mental ill health
are commonly portrayed in the media

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:08.959
both negatively and positively.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.659
This can be through news articles
both on TV and in newspapers, in films

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.029
and tv programmes both fictional and
non-fictional, on children's TV and

00:00:18.039 --> 00:00:20.160
also across digital and social media.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:24.120
Rhiannon: If mental health is shown
as a good news story with positive

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:28.980
endorsements, for example, fund raising
success, support and feel-good factors

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.110
such as ‘comic relief’, this will
influence people in a positive way and

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.649
they will remember the good things.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.890
Leah: If mental health is shown negatively
such as showing violence and bad

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:43.850
behaviour in a news article, documentary
or a storyline for a drama, this will

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.070
have negative influences on attitudes.

00:00:46.889 --> 00:00:51.059
Rhiannon: However, some media reporting,
even though the content shows negative

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:54.730
things, can have a positive effect
as it raises everyone’s awareness.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:59.450
Such as cases of abuse for
example, child neglect, human

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:03.890
trafficking, child endangerment
and child sexual exploitation.

00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:08.529
Leah: By this being shown widely
in the media, it can help encourage

00:01:08.549 --> 00:01:12.560
more people to come forward with
information and make more of the public

00:01:12.609 --> 00:01:16.600
open to discussion of these topics,
ultimately raising the profile of

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.870
mental health issues as a consequence.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:23.910
Rhiannon: Journalists, script writers
and other media professionals have to

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:28.250
ensure fictional and factual portrayals
of people with mental health problems

00:01:28.549 --> 00:01:31.210
in the media are accurate and sensitive.

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:35.280
Leah: More and more ‘bloggers'
and ‘vloggers' are now responding

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.950
to these portrayals, relaying
their own experiences and raising

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:42.430
awareness of the different attitudes
they have personally encountered.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:47.009
Rhiannon: Digital and social media
is a big part of most young peoples

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:50.820
lives and they can gain a lot of
positivity from what is out there,

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:55.530
however there is also a lot of
negativity carried in these formats too.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.550
Leah: If what children and young
people see online and how mental health

00:01:59.559 --> 00:02:03.919
issues are portrayed only leaves them
angry, sad, worried, stressed, or

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.990
annoyed, this can build up and start
having a negative impact on their

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:09.680
life and their own mental health.

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:13.240
Rhiannon: For example, they may
start worrying more about how they

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:15.250
look or what they’re missing out on.

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:20.829
A lot of people maintain an overly
idealised online presence or world, which

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:25.579
many others then fail to see as such,
instead struggling to keep a positive

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.839
view of their own lives by contrast.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.630
Leah: We cannot ignore the media
as individuals are continuously

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:36.609
consuming its output however we need
to be aware that the way things are

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:41.579
represented need to be realistic or for
a specific storyline and not used in

00:02:41.579 --> 00:02:45.970
a derogatory or flippant manner just
to make good TV or for sensationalism.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:50.280
Rhiannon: Mental health needs to be shown
appropriately and should be relevant

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.549
if society is to become more accepting.

